        "original_id": "b17ce59c-472e-50e9-922f-e784a745ab3d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jerry Buckner, Gary Garcia, Howard Cosell\n- Organizations: Billboard\n- Places: Akron, Ohio\n- Roles: bookmaker, gambler\n- Concepts: Vigorish, vig, juice, under-juice, the cut, the take\n- Projects: Buckner & Garcia, Willis the Guard & Vigorish\n\nFacts:\n- Buckner & Garcia was an American musical duo consisting of Jerry Buckner and Gary Garcia from Akron, Ohio.\n- Buckner & Garcia performed under the pseudonym Willis the Guard & Vigorish.\n- The song by Willis the Guard & Vigorish reached No. 82 on the Billboard charts despite limited airplay after Howard Cosell found the song offensive.\n- Vigorish, also called the vig, juice, under-juice, the cut, or the take, is the amount a bookmaker charges for taking a bet from a gambler.",
